│ the current year. It is currently:                                 │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  if year >= 0 and year <= 69:                                      │
│      # Interpret as 2000-2069                                      │
│  elif year >= 70 and year <= 99:                                   │
│      # Interpret as 1970-1999                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This logic is incorrect according to RFC 7231, which requires a    │
│ year comparison to determine the correct interpretation of a       │
│ two-digit year.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                  ✅ Step 3: Compare with RFC 7231                  │
│                                                                    │
│ RFC 7231 (Section 9.9.1) specifies that a two-digit year must be   │
│ interpreted as the most recent year in the past with the same last │
│ two digits. For example:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  • 00 → 2000                                                       │
│  • 69 → 2069                                                       │
│  • 70 → 1970                                                       │
│  • 99 → 1999                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The current logic does not compare the year to the current year,   │
│ leading to incorrect interpretations.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                             🛠️ Solution                             │
│                                                                    │
│ To fix the issue, update the year logic to compare the year to the │
│ current year:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  from datetime import datetime                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  def parse_http_date(date_str):                                    │
│      # Parse the date string into a datetime object                │
│      date_obj = datetime.strptime(date_str, "%a, %d %b %Y %H:%M:%  │
│  %Z")                                                              │
│      year = date_obj.year                                          │
│                                                                    │
│      # Compare with current year to determine the correct          │
│  interpretation                                                    │
│      if year >= 0 and year <= 69:                                  │
│          # Interpret as 2000-2069                                  │
│          return f"{year + 2000}"                                   │
│      elif year >= 70 and year <= 99:                               │
│          # Interpret as 1970-1999                                  │
│          return f"{year + 1970}"                                   │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                              📝 Notes                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • This solution assumes the date string is in the format "%a, %d  │
│    %b %Y %H:%M:%S %Z".                                             │
│  • The logic is not tied to the current year, but instead uses the │
